{
  "_comment": [
    "WHAT THE HOME PAGE SAYS WE DO, joined to what the catalogue can execute.",
    "",
    "These are the capability chips under each service on the home page. They",
    "were thirty hand-written strings in index.html: eight of them repeated a",
    "catalogue feature's name word for word, and twenty-two named nothing the",
    "system had ever heard of. A visitor cannot tell the difference, and",
    "neither could an agent — which is the problem. A string that reads like a",
    "capability and resolves to nothing is worse than no string at all.",
    "",
    "So every chip now declares what it is:",
    "",
    "  feature   one catalogue feature executes it       -> featureId",
    "  group     several features together are it        -> featureIds",
    "  platform  a platform an existing feature runs on  -> featureId + platformId",
    "  marketing copy, and nothing executes it           -> reason",
    "",
    "`marketing` is a legitimate answer and is meant to be used. What is not",
    "legitimate is leaving the question unanswered, so build-catalogue.js",
    "refuses a chip with no type, a featureId that resolves to nothing, a",
    "featureId belonging to another service, or a `marketing` chip that gives",
    "no reason.",
    "",
    "index.html no longer holds these words. tools/build-capabilities.js",
    "renders them from here, in both languages, in the order below."
  ],
